      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Clinical findings upon examination of advanced-age patients with ischemic heart disease and bronchial asthma demonstrated evident phasic changes in the course of IHD dependent on aggravation or remission of the asthma. Exacerbations of bronchial asthma are accompanied by attenuation of clinical and ECG manifestations of IHD whereas the arrest of the bronchoobstructive syndrome leads to return of the cardiac symptoms. The relationship may arise due to transitory metabolic abnormalities of cyclic nucleotides."},
